kourin shown house in prison in  northeastern berlin embodies the 44  years of political persecution in former  East Germany among the thousands of  prisoners to pass through its gates was  83 year old honored rifki who served  five and a half years there that was the  worst time this little cell here was  isolated with no one to speak to except  the interrogator i was completely closed  off from the outside world no other  prisoner to see no letter no newspaper  no book in 1953 the their 19 year old  was imprisoned for military and economic  espionage inmates were often subjected  to physical and psychological torture to  extract information then there were the  night interrogations which were  constantly carried out so you had no  sleep and sleeping during the day was  impossible - after three days my nerves  were through and I told the interrogator  everything the Stasi was the most  important instrument and enforcing the  communist dictatorship in former East  Germany five decades after his release  Arno has many unanswered questions not  least of all why his arrest warrant was  signed by someone as high up as a vice  Stasi Minister after the fall of the  wall I saw my arrest warrant for the  first time and I was astonished that it  was signed by Erich Mielke and that it  was marked as a secret classified  document why is this the case this  wasn't another arrest warrants and why  did I get a single cell in 1962 just a  year after the construction of the wall  dividing East and West Germany Arno was  unexpectedly released due to the need  for more prison spaces his deepest  regret is the lost decade of his youth  1992 was the first time I was here again  as it was open to the public I drove  here with my wife but then I took a turn  for the worse I had nightmares at night  that they were arresting me again I had  screaming Fitz and my wife often had to  wake me up Christian  Padma Kofi freakin mission more than  five decades since his release the  memories of Horan Shirin Heusen remain  vivid but consequent visits with family  and tours with schoolchildren have acted  as therapy but some things will never be  regained
 

